hey guys it's angelico with max tech and  i've been using the airpods pro  for over a year now and today i want to  talk about my experience with them  give you my personal thoughts and  opinions and let you know about the one  big disappointment i have with these  earbuds  first i want to talk about the case this  case is fantastic  it feels great it's really high quality  and  it's the most compact and comfortable  case in my opinion the hinge is amazing  and to this day it's the best hinge out  of any wireless earbud case  the samsung's hinges are pretty awful  honestly especially the older bun models  along with that all the galaxy buds  cases don't feel nearly as premium they  feel very cheap in comparison  the magnet in the case holding the  airpods is really strong and secure you  can drop the air pods in and they'll  snap in perfectly  unlike most galaxy buds cases that have  a much weaker magnet  making the buds feel not very secure the  case also comes with wireless charging  which is great the amber charging light  turns on very quickly  much faster than the samsung galaxy buds  which take like twice as long  this isn't super important but it's kind  of a pet peeve of mine  now talking about the design and comfort  i love how these look  i know that a lot of people think that  they look pretty dumb but  i personally think they look great in  high quality they're also  extremely comfortable these are the only  truly comfortable buds that i've tried i  forget i even have them  in all of the samsung earbuds hurt my  ears  especially the ceilings i wanted to test  out the galaxy beds pro for a week and  see how they compare to these airpods  pro that i use  every day but they were so incredibly  uncomfortable for me  that i couldn't even wear them for more  than a couple minutes  i have very small ears so that's  definitely why  they were totally fine for max and he  actually really enjoys samsung's earbuds  but unfortunately they're just not for  me so if you're like me and have small  ears  i'd for sure say get the airpods pro  another feature that makes these so  comfortable  is the built-in vent that equalizes  pressure so you don't get that suction  feeling in your ears  the tips are also super easy to replace  and they're super secure  my only complaint about comfort are the  stems  they always get in the way and fall out  when you're changing your shirt  they're also pretty uncomfortable when  you're laying down on your side  which sucks because i love using these  air paws in bed  now moving on to controls the pressure  sensitive stem is amazing  it's super easy to use and it's very  consistent i hate other brands methods  of touch controls the galaxy butts pro  were so  frustrating for me because anytime i  would try to adjust the buds  it would pause my music or skip tracks  so you can't even touch them so i had a  terrible personal experience with those  and they made me appreciate these  airpods even more  now i really don't want to sound like an  apple sheep but this is honestly how i  feel pairing is super easy and quick  it's really easy to switch between  devices and really easy to reset these  air pods if need be  the microphone quality is really good  i've asked people how i sound  and they always say that i sound loud  and clear here's my comparison for you  guys  let me know what you think this is the  microphone quality with apple's airpods  pro  this is a microphone quality that you  can expect with samsung's new  galaxy buds pro this is the microphone  quality of the galaxy buds plus  a nice upgrade with these compared to  the previous airpods  is water resistance these have an ipx4  water resistance rating  so they're fully sweat proof and have  water resistance i've dropped them in  the water once or twice for a split  second  and thank goodness they were totally  fine however with the previous airpods  i dropped one in the water for a split  second and it was completely ruined  so these being able to withstand some  water is really great  however the newest galaxy buds pro have  a rating of ipx7  which means that they are fully  waterproof and can be in a meter of  water  for up to 30 minutes and be totally fine  which is awesome  so if waterproofing is a concern for you  you might want to consider galaxy butts  for peace of mind  now let's get into noise cancellation  and transparency mode the noise  cancellation is really good  it gets rid of almost all the low  rumbling noise you can still hear  some of the higher frequency sounds but  if you're playing music with this mode  on you won't hear  anything and with that anc also  increases audio quality  since other sounds can get in the way so  your listening experience is definitely  heightened for me personally  i get anxiety when i can't hear and be  aware of my surroundings  so perfect anc isn't something i'm  honestly too  interested in i can't imagine the ansi  disappointing anyone  unless you work with like a jackhammer  every day or something  the transparency mode is also honestly  pretty good everything sounds  really realistic and normal and i use  this mode  all the time and love it now i'm no  audiophile but the sound quality is  really good to me i was amazed the first  time i used them  the mids and highs are great the only  thing it possibly lacks  are the lows the base is a little weak  especially compared to the galaxy buds  pro  which have a nice loud base but it  obviously comes down to personal  preference and  what kind of music you're listening to  now let's talk about the main  disappointment that i have with these  airpods  and that is battery life these will give  you about  five hours of consistent playback with  anc enabled  now i don't use anc mode that often so  i'm usually in transparency mode which  uses less battery  however the battery life still isn't  good  for me and my use patterns if i'm using  these air pods  i'm usually using them for long periods  of time i'll put these in at full  battery and use them until they  eventually die  and then i have to stop and charge them  before i can continue what i was doing  i really do wish the battery life was a  bit better luckily  charging doesn't take long five minutes  in the case gives you an hour of  listening time  now let's talk about the price 250  is pretty expensive for a pair of  earbuds but  honestly they're so worth it i was  slightly hesitant to purchase them  because of the price  but i was so happy i did and i don't  regret it for a second  these airpods were one of my best and  most worth it investments  these have everything i want in a pair  of wireless earbuds they sound amazing  and they're so  incredibly comfortable the battery life  isn't great but charging them up in the  case is super fast  it's not too much of an inconvenience if  you're looking to buy a pair of wireless  earbuds  these are definitely amazing and i doubt  they will disappoint  however you might want to wait a little  bit because apple is going to be  releasing airpods pro 2  this year and i want to quickly go over  the leaks and rumors we've been hearing  about them  mark german claimed that these airpods  pro 2 will come with a brand new  circular design and an upgraded wireless  chip if they do drop the stem  that would be amazing and i could see a  lot of people  buying them just for that especially  since a lot of people don't enjoy the  look of the stems  this design could also allow for a  bigger battery so  we would probably see battery life  improvements which would be really great  apple in october was granted a patent  for in-air  gesture input for airpods so if the new  airpods pro 2  won't come out with a stem this  technology would actually make sense  and it would be better than touch  controls since the experience with those  on the buds pro for example  isn't great they also included a couple  of other ideas  like putting in a tactile structure like  a crown on the airpods themselves  ming chi kuo claimed that the airpods  pro 2 will be coming in april  may or june of 2021. there are also a  lot of rumors about the new airpods gen  3 coming out so check out vadim's leaks  and rumors video  he's compiled a lot of very interesting  information if you guys are wondering  about the upcoming airpods  so if you're interested in buying a pair  of airpods pro earbuds  you should probably wait for the new  ones to come out but also remember that  these airpods pro are currently on sale  for 220 bucks and the price will  probably drop  even more when the new ones come out  thank you guys for watching let me know  your thoughts and if you guys are  excited about the new upcoming airpods  too  click the button above to subscribe and  check out one of those two videos over  there  this has been angelic with maxtec and it  will see you in the next one  you
 

